      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just a poetic way to ignore the logic. if the \"texture\" is just a momentary sensory input that eventually ends anyway, it doesn't change the outcome. if the net value of an existence that is mostly suffering and eventually ends is zero, then the decision to end it early is just a way to resolve the equation. it's a neutral move. why is it considered \"wrong\" to just accept the math and stop the process?",
